{
  "_doc": {
    "about": "Search field chips and completion every client must match: web (shared/src/search.ts) and Android :core. Offsets are UTF-16 code units, like JavaScript and Kotlin strings.",
    "parse": "parseQuery(text, cursor). Tokens split at whitespace outside \"quotes\" and (…)/{…} groups. A token is a chip when it is [-]operator:value with a known operator (case-insensitive, stored lower-case), a non-empty value that is either bare (no quotes or brackets) or one closed \"quoted\" value (stored without quotes, trimmed), every quote and group closed, and the cursor not inside or touching it (cursor < start or > end). A token right before or after a token that is exactly 'OR' (upper-case, top level) never becomes a chip, so the operator keeps its place in the OR. A chip is removed with the whitespace up to the next token; the last token is removed with trailing whitespace if any, else with the whitespace before it (back to the previous token, or the previous removal). cursor in the result is mapped into free (one inside removed text moves to where that text was); with cursor null it is free.length and context is null. context: the token with start <= cursor <= end (or, when none, {operator, prefix '', start = end = cursor}); typed = token text up to the cursor; a leading '-' sets negated. No ':' in typed: operator context if the rest is letters/underscores (prefix = rest; end = just after the token's colon if it has one, else the token end), else null. With ':': the name must be an operator (else null); prefix = what follows, an opening quote dropped; value = all the token holds after its colon, past the cursor too, an opening quote dropped; null if it then holds a quote or bracket; start/end = the whole token. With tags (the search field), a token that is one whole #tag as todos have them (optionally after -) is a chip too, operator \"#\" and the tag's name as its value; without, it stays free text.",
    "format": "formatChip: [-]operator:value; the value in double quotes (inner quotes dropped) when it holds whitespace, a quote or a bracket. A tag chip ({operator: \"#\"}) is [-]#name.",
    "query": "queryText(chips, free): formatted chips then trimmed free text, joined by single spaces, empties left out.",
    "completions": "completions(context, { now, timeZone, labels, contacts }). Operators: OPERATORS in order whose name starts with prefix (case-insensitive); label and value 'name:', detail OPERATOR_DETAILS. Fixed lists (in, is, has, category, larger/smaller/size, older_than/newer_than) filtered by prefix on value (ages also on label); detail null. after/before: today, yesterday, last week = 0, 1, 7 calendar days back from now's date in timeZone, value yyyy/mm/dd, detail = value, kept when label or value starts with prefix. label: names whose labelQueryValue (lower-case, runs of whitespace or '/' as '-') starts with prefix, or with any part (split on whitespace and '/') starting with it; value labelQueryValue(name). from/to/cc/bcc/deliveredto: contacts whose email or name starts with prefix, or any name word does; label name (or email when nameless), value email, detail email (null when nameless). Labels and contacts keep the caller's order, at most 8. Other operators: none. With nothing typed, operators are only from, to, subject, has and is.",
    "apply": "applyCompletion(text, context, candidate). Operator: replace [start, end) with ('-' if negated) + value; cursor after it. Value: replace [start, end) with formatChip({operator, value, negated}) plus a space unless the text after already starts with whitespace; cursor one past the chip.",
    "unchip": "unchip(chips, index, free): chip removed; free = its formatted text, then a space and the left-trimmed free text when that is non-empty; cursor = formatted length.",
    "local": "isLocalChip: is:snoozed, is:todo and in:outbox (value case-insensitive, negated or not).",
    "help": "The search help both apps list: every operator in OPERATORS order, its detail (OPERATOR_DETAILS) and one example (OPERATOR_EXAMPLES); common is COMMON_OPERATORS. own is OWN_TERMS: our own terms and what each lists.",
    "awaitsValue": "awaitsValue(parseQuery(text, cursor).context): true when the context is a value with nothing after the colon, past the cursor too (an operator alone, or only an opening quote). There Enter completes the highlighted suggestion, else the first, else searches without that operator (withoutOperator); elsewhere Enter searches unless a suggestion is highlighted.",
    "withoutOperator": "withoutOperator(free, parseQuery(text, cursor).context): the free text with the operator under the cursor taken out, one space left between the words either side.",
    "gmailQuery": "gmailQueryText(chips, free): queryText with the local chips left out, is:pinned as is:starred, is:done as -in:inbox and -is:done as in:inbox."
  },
